rÆ␀␀␀c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ó¢␀␀␀—␀	␀|␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|«␀␀␀␀␀␀S␀#␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀$␀r2␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|␀d¬«␀␀␀␀␀␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|«␀␀␀␀␀␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀«␀␀␀␀␀␀cY␀S␀w␀xY␀w)aˆ␀␀
    Permute the dimensions of an array.

    This function is exactly equivalent to `numpy.transpose`.

    See Also
    --------
    numpy.transpose : Equivalent function in top-level NumPy module.

    Examples
    --------
    >>> import numpy.ma as ma
    >>> x = ma.arange(4).reshape((2,2))
    >>> x[1, 1] = ma.masked
    >>> x
    masked_array(
      data=[[0, 1],
            [2, --]],
      mask=[[False, False],
            [False,  True]],
      fill_value=999999)

    >>> ma.transpose(x)
    masked_array(
      data=[[0, 2],
            [1, --]],
      mask=[[False, False],
            [False,  True]],
      fill_value=999999)
